       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg daily is twice the maximum labeled sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify going above that. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects.\n\nPlease tell me which of these applies:\n- **Typo or wrong dose:** If you meant 200 mg once daily (or 40 mg, or another dose), tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Titration:** If you want to start lower and increase, I can enter a starting dose such as 50 mg once daily. Typical increases are 25\u201350 mg at weekly intervals, up to 200 mg.\n- **Intentional supratherapeutic dose:** If you really want 400 mg, for example as part of a specialist-directed plan, confirm that explicitly and give a short rationale for the order note. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy. Because this exceeds the standard limit, I'd like your confirmation before I place it."
      }
     ],
